# Purpose: dl_iterate_phdr's single-image (no-dynamic-link-segment) fallback derives the
#   load bias solely from a PT_PHDR program header; GNU ld emits no PT_PHDR for static
#   non-PIE executables, so the for-else hits `unreachable` and the process panics.
#   Measured: x86_64 `gcc -static -no-pie -fuse-ld=bfd` -> 10 program headers, no PHDR;
#   dynamic PIE control -> 13 headers, PHDR present at 0x40. For ET_EXEC non-PIE the bias
#   IS zero, and the existing expression already evaluates to zero whenever PT_PHDR is
#   present, so any image that has one (all PIE/dynamic images do) is unaffected.
# Affects: lib/std/posix.zig (fn dl_iterate_phdr, dl_phdr_info struct literal)
# Upstream: not filed
# Drop-when: upstream zig fixes dl_iterate_phdr to tolerate a missing PT_PHDR
#   (bias 0 for ET_EXEC non-PIE)
# Last-verified: 2026-09-07 / snapshot 2033+af24fd11a
#
# Defect is unchanged across 149 snapshots: identical expression at identical line
# numbers 818-821 in both 1884+841dd0eb8 and 2033+af24fd11a.
#
# Consequence in this recipe: the caller is debug/SelfInfo/Elf.zig findModule, so
# module lookup fails; the panic fires inside the stack-trace printer while it holds
# the stderr lock, the recursive panic re-enters that non-recursive lock, and the
# process deadlocks in futex forever. On linux-ppc64le (final links go through LLD,
# no GCC-driver redirect), this is the confirmed mechanism behind the Phase 2
# langref hang at the 6h CI ceiling:
# langref runs doc/langref/stack_trace.zig, whose @panic exists precisely to print a
# stack trace.

--- a/lib/std/posix.zig
+++ b/lib/std/posix.zig
@@ -818,7 +818,7 @@
             .addr = for (phdrs) |phdr| switch (phdr.type) {
                 .PHDR => break @intFromPtr(phdrs.ptr) - phdr.vaddr,
                 else => {},
-            } else unreachable,
+            } else 0,
             .name = switch (getauxval(std.elf.AT_EXECFN)) {
                 0 => "/proc/self/exe",
                 else => |name| @ptrFromInt(name),
